{
  "text": "```systemverilog\nmodule rstgen (\n    input  logic clk_i,\n    input  logic rst_ni,\n    input  logic test_mode_i,\n    output logic rst_no,\n    output logic init_no\n);\n\n    // Synchronization chain for reset release\n    logic [1:0] sync_rst;\n\n    // Initialize to reset state (active-low = 0)\n    // On power-up, we want rst_no to be 0 (reset asserted)\n    // The sync chain should start at 0 and transition to 1 when rst_ni goes high\n\n    // Synchronize the reset input\n    always_ff @(posedge clk_i) begin\n        sync_rst[0] <= rst_ni;\n        sync_rst[1] <= sync_rst[0];\n    end\n\n    // In test mode, bypass synchronization\n    assign rst_no = test_mode_i ? rst_ni : sync_rst[1];\n\n    // init_no: short initialization qualifier after reset release\n    // init_no should be low for a few cycles after rst_no releases, then go high\n    // Use a small counter or shift register to generate a pulse\n\n    logic [2:0] init_cnt;\n\n    always_ff @(posedge clk_i) begin\n        if (!rst_no) begin\n            init_cnt <= 3'd0;\n        end else if (init_cnt < 3'd3) begin\n            init_cnt <= init_cnt + 3'd1;\n        end\n    end\n\n    // init_no is high when initialization is complete\n    assign init_no = (init_cnt == 3'd3);\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
